{%- comment -%}
  PG Unlock: the cart's Buy 2 Get 1 Free row -- plus two cart repairs that have
  no better home.

  WHY THREE THINGS ARE IN ONE FILE. They belong in their own sections and were
  written that way twice. Neither survived, for two compounding reasons:

    1. A section group holds a MAXIMUM OF 25 SECTIONS. footer-group is at the
       cap. themeFilesUpsert validates on write, so a 26th is rejected outright
       -- but a group sitting AT the limit renders only the first entries and
       silently drops the tail. New sections were accepted, reported correctly
       by the API, and never appeared on the page.

    2. footer-group.json is rewritten by the theme EDITOR. Every save in the
       customiser rebuilds that file from the editor's own state, which does
       not know about sections added through the API -- so a newly registered
       section is dropped again the next time the theme is opened.

  pg-unlock is in overlay-group and has been registered for weeks, so it
  renders and the editor leaves it alone. That is the whole reason this is
  here. If footer-group ever gets a free slot, lift sections 2 and 3 back out.

  ================================================================
  1. THE OFFER ROW

  The rung is the quantity that EARNS the discount and the free unit is the one
  after it, so Buy 2 Get 1 Free is only real once the cart holds three. The
  button adds however many units that takes, and the copy says it the way the
  shopper experiences it -- they pay for one more and two arrive:

      1 orb ..... Buy 1 more, get 1 FREE   (adds 2, charges 1)
      2 orbs .... Add your FREE 3rd Orb    (adds 1, charges 0)
      3 orbs .... offer taken, no row

  CHOOSING THE DESIGNS. On a product with more than one design -- the orb, whose
  character IS the product -- the button no longer adds more of the variant
  already in the cart. It opens a chooser: one dropdown per unit the offer adds,
  each defaulted to a design the shopper is not already holding, and the units
  go in as separate line items so every one keeps its own picker in the cart.
  Buying three orbs is meant to be three characters; adding three of the one
  they picked, on a single merged line with a single picker, was the opposite of
  the offer. Different variants of the same product all qualify for that
  product's BXGY, so a mixed three still pays out the free one. Single-design
  products (the wall art, and the console when it has one variant) skip the
  chooser and add directly, exactly as before.

  ================================================================
  2. THE STRUCK PRICE IN THE STEPPER

  The line is a grid: "nm nm" / "vr vr" / "sv sv" / "qt pr" -- stepper in `qt`,
  price in `pr`. Separate cells, so nothing should collide.

  What collides is the CONTENT of `pr`. nc-linesave draws the price as a flex
  ROW with white-space:nowrap: .nc-lsave-was (struck), .nc-lsave-now (charged),
  .nc-lsave-off (pill). nowrap means it cannot break, and a grid item's default
  min-width:auto means it will not shrink below its content -- so once was +
  now is wider than the column it overflows LEFT into `qt` and the struck
  figure lands on the + button.

  Stacked into a column, struck figure first. NO media query: the drawer is
  ~380-420px wide on desktop too, which is where it was also reported.
  min-width:0 matters as much as the direction.

  ================================================================
  3. THE DRAWER MARK

  The disc was hidden in CSS in one file and replaced by JS in another. When
  only the hide arrived the cart had NO mark at all -- worse than the disc. So
  the hide happens in JS, on the line after the wordmark is inserted: if
  anything fails, the disc simply stays. Stamped inline because pe-logo,
  pg-drawer and nc-recs all write that element with !important and up to three
  ids.

  The mark is <a class="pg-wordmark"> so pg-wordmark kerns it -- that file
  splits the T into its own span, which is what stops it reading POCKE T ERA.
  Inheriting the class also inherits pg-mobile's HEADER sizing (clamp to 78px,
  scaleY(2.6), negative letter-spacing, all !important), so each of those is
  re-set below on a doubled id.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  #cart .pg-unlock{
    display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;
    flex-wrap:wrap;          /* the chooser panel is flex:1 1 100% -- without wrap
                                at EVERY width it cannot drop to its own line, so
                                on the ~485px desktop drawer it sat beside the
                                copy and crushed the title to one word per line */
    margin:10px 0 4px;padding:11px 13px;
    border:1px solid rgba(122,47,162,.3);border-radius:14px;
    background:linear-gradient(120deg,#F8F3FC,#F1E7F8);
    box-shadow:0 12px 30px -24px rgba(74,28,102,.45);
    font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;
  }
  #cart .pg-unlock img{width:52px;height:52px;border-radius:10px;object-fit:cover;flex:none;background:#efe4f8}
  #cart .pg-unlock-t{flex:1;min-width:0}
  #cart .pg-unlock-t b{display:block;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.3;color:#3B1553}
  #cart .pg-unlock-t small{display:block;font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.35;color:#6E5C80;margin-top:2px}
  #cart .pg-unlock-tag{
    display:inline-block;margin-top:4px;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:999px;
    font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:#fff;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#9B4BC4,#7A2FA2);
  }
  #cart .pg-unlock-add{
    flex:none;border:1.5px solid #7A2FA2 !important;background:#fff !important;
    background-image:none !important;color:#7A2FA2 !important;
    border-radius:999px !important;padding:9px 18px !important;
    font-family:inherit;font-weight:800;font-size:13px;cursor:pointer;
    animation:none !important;transition:background .15s ease,color .15s ease;
  }
  #cart .pg-unlock-add::before,#cart .pg-unlock-add::after{display:none !important;content:none !important}
  #cart .pg-unlock-add:hover{background:linear-gradient(120deg,#9B4BC4,#7A2FA2) !important;color:#fff !important}
  #cart .pg-unlock-add[disabled]{opacity:.6;cursor:default}
  /* MOBILE PARITY: the row keeps the same three parts in the same order as
     desktop -- image, copy, button -- the button simply drops to its own full
     width line instead of shrinking the copy to nothing. */
  @media(max-width:600px){
    #cart .pg-unlock{flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px}
    #cart .pg-unlock img{width:46px;height:46px}
    #cart .pg-unlock-t{flex:1 1 60%;min-width:0}
    #cart .pg-unlock-t b{font-size:13px}
    #cart .pg-unlock-t small{font-size:11.5px}
    #cart .pg-unlock-add{flex:1 1 100%;order:4;padding:11px 18px !important;font-size:13.5px}
  }

  /* ---------------- the design chooser ----------------
     The upsell used to add more of the variant already in the cart. On the orb
     that is the wrong unit: the character IS the product, and Shopify merges
     identical variants onto one line with one picker, so a shopper handed three
     of what they picked could not change any of them. The button now opens this
     panel -- one select per unit the offer adds -- and posts them as separate
     lines so each keeps its own picker in the cart. */
  #cart .pg-unlock-pick{
    flex:1 1 100%;display:none;margin:2px 0 0;padding:10px 0 0;
    border-top:1px solid rgba(122,47,162,.18);
  }
  #cart .pg-unlock.is-open .pg-unlock-pick{display:block}
  /* once the panel is open the trigger button has done its job, and the panel's
     own "Add ... to cart" is the CTA -- two buttons that both add is confusing,
     and on the narrow drawer the trigger was overlapping the title. Hide it and
     let the copy take the full first line. */
  #cart .pg-unlock.is-open .pg-unlock-add{display:none !important}
  #cart .pg-unlock.is-open .pg-unlock-tag{display:none}
  #cart .pg-unlock.is-open .pg-unlock-t{flex:1 1 100%}
  #cart .pg-unlock-pick-r{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin:0 0 7px}
  #cart .pg-unlock-pick-r span{
    flex:none;width:58px;
    font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.03em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A2FA2;
  }
  #cart .pg-unlock-pick select{
    flex:1;min-width:0;-webkit-appearance:menulist;appearance:menulist;
    padding:8px 10px;border:1.5px solid rgba(122,47,162,.35);border-radius:10px;
    background:#fff;color:#3B1553;font-family:inherit;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;
  }
  #cart .pg-unlock-pick select:focus{outline:2px solid #9B4BC4;outline-offset:1px}
  #cart .pg-unlock-go{
    width:100%;margin-top:3px;border:0 !important;border-radius:999px !important;padding:12px 16px !important;
    background:linear-gradient(120deg,#9B4BC4,#7A2FA2) !important;
    background-image:linear-gradient(120deg,#9B4BC4,#7A2FA2) !important;
    color:#fff !important;font-family:inherit;font-weight:800;font-size:13.5px;cursor:pointer;animation:none !important;
  }
  #cart .pg-unlock-go::before,#cart .pg-unlock-go::after{display:none !important;content:none !important}
  #cart .pg-unlock-go[disabled]{opacity:.6;cursor:default}
  @media(max-width:600px){
    #cart .pg-unlock-pick-r span{width:50px;font-size:10.5px}
    #cart .pg-unlock-pick select{font-size:12.5px;padding:9px 9px}
  }

  /* ---------------- the slot: visual order pinned in CSS ----------------
     The screen recording showed the two offer rows SWAPPING places. Every
     defence inside render() still left one dependency: the rows' on-screen
     order was their DOM order, and anything that reinserted them -- a stale
     cached copy of an older script, a drawer rebuild racing a render -- could
     flip it. So the rows now live in one flex container and each product's
     row carries a fixed CSS `order`. DOM order no longer decides anything:
     whatever writes the rows, in whatever sequence, the screen shows wall art,
     then console, then orb. A swap is not suppressed; it is impossible. */
  #cart #pg-unlock-slot{display:flex;flex-direction:column}
  #cart #pg-unlock-slot .pg-unlock[data-pg-unlock*="anime"]{order:0}
  #cart #pg-unlock-slot .pg-unlock[data-pg-unlock*="handheld"]{order:1}
  #cart #pg-unlock-slot .pg-unlock[data-pg-unlock*="pokemon"]{order:2}

  /* ---------------- 2. the struck price keeps to its own cell ---------------- */
  html body #cart .l4ca > li section .nc-lsave,
  html body #cart .l4ca > li section .price,
  html body #cart .l4ca > li section .cols .price{
    min-width:0 !important;
    max-width:100% !important;
    display:flex !important;
    flex-direction:column !important;
    flex-wrap:nowrap !important;
    align-items:flex-end !important;
    justify-content:flex-end !important;
    gap:1px !important;
    text-align:right !important;
    overflow:visible !important;
  }
  html body #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave .nc-lsave-was,
  html body #cart .l4ca > li .price .old-price,
  html body #cart .l4ca > li .price s,
  html body #cart .l4ca > li .price del{
    order:-1 !important;
    display:block !important;
    margin:0 !important;
    font-size:12px !important;
    font-weight:600 !important;
    line-height:1.15 !important;
    white-space:nowrap !important;
  }
  html body #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave .nc-lsave-now{
    order:0 !important;line-height:1.2 !important;white-space:nowrap !important;
  }
  html body #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave .nc-lsave-off{
    order:1 !important;margin-top:2px !important;
  }
  html body #cart .l4ca > li section footer{min-width:0 !important;flex-wrap:wrap !important}

  /* ---------------- 3. the drawer mark ---------------- */
  #cart .pg-cart-mark{
    display:block;background:#0B0710;border-radius:12px;
    padding:13px 14px 10px;margin:0 0 8px;text-align:center;overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 8px 22px -18px rgba(0,0,0,.8);
  }
  html body #cart#cart a.pg-cart-word{
    display:inline-block !important;
    font-family:'Press Start 2P','Courier New',monospace !important;
    font-weight:400 !important;
    font-size:13px !important;
    line-height:1 !important;
    letter-spacing:0 !important;
    white-space:nowrap !important;
    max-width:100% !important;
    margin:0 !important;padding:0 !important;
    color:#F6DBFF !important;
    text-decoration:none !important;
    transform:scaleY(1.5) !important;
    transform-origin:center !important;
    text-shadow:0 0 5px rgba(246,219,255,.45),0 0 14px rgba(199,155,234,.32) !important;
  }
  @media(max-width:600px){
    #cart .pg-cart-mark{padding:11px 10px 9px}
    html body #cart#cart a.pg-cart-word{font-size:11px !important}
  }
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgUnlock) return; window.pgUnlock = 1;

  var LADDERS = {
    'pokemon-crystal-ball-3d-pikachu-gengar-mewtwo-night-light-lamp-pokeball-3d-glass-pokemon-crystal-ball-statue-kids-birthday-gift': {
      name: 'Crystal PokeOrb',
      rungs: {2: {pct: 100, nth: '3rd'}}
    },
    'anime-pokemon-3d-lenticular-poster-charizard-squirtle-bulbasaur-come-alive-with-amazing-3d-effects-wall-art-printwithout-frame': {
      name: 'Heroic Holographic Wall Art',
      rungs: {2: {pct: 100, nth: '3rd'}}
    },
    'handheld-game-console': {
      name: 'PocketBoy R36',
      rungs: {1: {pct: 25, nth: '2nd'}}
    }
  };

  var busy = false;
  var lastKey = '';

  function money(c){ return '$' + (c / 100).toFixed(2); }

  /* ---------------- one line per variant ---------------- */
  var merging = false;
  var merges = 0;
  var mergedVariants = {};
  var MAX_MERGES = 4;

  function consolidate(cart){
    if (merging) return false;

    /* CONVERGENCE GUARD -- read this before removing it.
       A BXGY allocation legitimately wants a variant on two lines. Merge them
       and Shopify splits them again on the next read, this fires on the next
       tick, and the cart thrashes. So a variant is merged AT MOST ONCE per
       page load, and MAX_MERGES caps attempts regardless.

       The chooser posts DIFFERENT variants, so its lines never collide here --
       this only ever merges accidental duplicates of one variant. */
    if (merges >= MAX_MERGES) return false;

    var byVariant = {};
    (cart.items || []).forEach(function(it){
      if (it.properties && it.properties._free_gift) return;
      (byVariant[it.variant_id] = byVariant[it.variant_id] || []).push(it);
    });

    var dupes = null;
    Object.keys(byVariant).forEach(function(v){
      if (dupes) return;
      if (byVariant[v].length < 2) return;
      if (mergedVariants[v]) return;
      dupes = byVariant[v];
      mergedVariants[v] = 1;
    });
    if (!dupes) return false;
    merges++;

    var total = dupes.reduce(function(n, it){ return n + it.quantity; }, 0);
    var keep = dupes[0];
    var drop = dupes.slice(1);

    merging = true;
    var chain = change(keep.key, total);
    drop.forEach(function(it){
      chain = chain.then(function(){ return change(it.key, 0); });
    });
    chain.then(function(){
      merging = false;
      lastKey = '';
      if (window.pgDrawerRefresh) return window.pgDrawerRefresh();
    }).then(function(){
      render();
    }).catch(function(){
      merging = false;
    });
    return true;
  }

  function change(key, qty){
    return fetch('/cart/change.js', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
      body: JSON.stringify({id: key, quantity: qty})
    });
  }

  function offers(cart){
    var byHandle = {};
    (cart.items || []).forEach(function(it){
      if (!LADDERS[it.handle]) return;
      if (it.properties && it.properties._free_gift) return;
      var h = byHandle[it.handle] || (byHandle[it.handle] = {qty: 0, item: it});
      h.qty += it.quantity;
    });
    var out = [];
    Object.keys(byHandle).forEach(function(handle){
      var rec = byHandle[handle];
      var rungs = LADDERS[handle].rungs;
      var rung = rungs[rec.qty];
      var at = rec.qty;

      if (!rung){
        var best = null;
        Object.keys(rungs).forEach(function(k){
          var q = parseInt(k, 10);
          if (q > rec.qty && (best === null || q < best)) best = q;
        });
        if (best === null) return;
        rung = rungs[best];
        at = best;
      }

      var need = (at + 1) - rec.qty;
      if (need < 1) return;

      out.push({
        handle: handle,
        name: LADDERS[handle].name,
        variant: rec.item.variant_id,
        key: rec.item.key,
        lineQty: rec.item.quantity,
        totalQty: rec.qty,
        image: rec.item.image,
        price: rec.item.price,
        rung: rung,
        need: need
      });
    });
    return out;
  }

  /* ---------------- the product's designs ----------------
     Fetched once per product and cached. Only AVAILABLE variants are offered:
     a chooser that lets someone pick a sold-out orb turns a completed offer
     into a failed add, which is the worst place to lose them. */
  var VCACHE = {}, VBUSY = {};
  function variantsFor(handle){
    if (VCACHE[handle]) return Promise.resolve(VCACHE[handle]);
    if (VBUSY[handle]) return VBUSY[handle];
    VBUSY[handle] = fetch('/products/' + handle + '.js')
      .then(function(r){ return r.json(); })
      .then(function(pr){
        var list = (pr.variants || []).filter(function(v){ return v.available !== false; })
          .map(function(v){ return {id: v.id, title: v.title}; });
        VCACHE[handle] = list;
        VBUSY[handle] = null;
        return list;
      })
      .catch(function(){ VBUSY[handle] = null; return []; });
    return VBUSY[handle];
  }

  /* Which designs are already in the cart, so the chooser defaults to ones the
     shopper does not have -- defaulting to duplicates would recreate the bug
     this replaces, just with a dropdown in front of it. */
  var LASTCART = {};
  function heldVariants(handle){
    var held = {};
    (LASTCART.items || []).forEach(function(it){
      if (it.handle === handle) held[it.variant_id] = true;
    });
    return held;
  }

  function buildChooser(el, o){
    var panel = el.querySelector('.pg-unlock-pick');
    if (!panel) return Promise.resolve(false);
    if (panel.dataset.built) return Promise.resolve(true);
    return variantsFor(o.handle).then(function(list){
      /* one design (wall art, single-variant console): nothing to choose */
      if (list.length < 2) return false;
      var held = heldVariants(o.handle);
      var fresh = list.filter(function(v){ return !held[v.id]; });
      var pool = fresh.length >= o.need ? fresh : list;

      var html = '';
      for (var i = 0; i < o.need; i++){
        var pick = pool[i % pool.length];
        var label = (o.rung.pct === 100 && i === o.need - 1) ? 'Free' : 'Pick ' + (i + 1);
        html += '<div class="pg-unlock-pick-r"><span>' + label + '</span><select data-i="' + i + '">';
        for (var j = 0; j < list.length; j++){
          html += '<option value="' + list[j].id + '"' +
                  (list[j].id === pick.id ? ' selected' : '') + '>' +
                  String(list[j].title).replace(/</g, '&lt;') + '</option>';
        }
        html += '</select></div>';
      }
      html += '<button type="button" class="pg-unlock-go">Add ' + o.need +
              (o.need === 1 ? ' orb' : '') + ' to cart' +
              (o.rung.pct === 100 ? ' - 1 is FREE' : '') + '</button>';
      panel.innerHTML = html;
      panel.dataset.built = '1';
      return true;
    });
  }

  function row(o){
    var el = document.createElement('div');
    el.className = 'pg-unlock';
    el.setAttribute('data-pg-unlock', o.handle);
    var free = o.rung.pct === 100;
    var after = free ? 'free' : money(Math.round(o.price * (100 - o.rung.pct) / 100));
    var img = o.image ? String(o.image).replace(/(\.[a-z]+)(\?|$)/i, '_120x$1$2') : '';

    var title, note;
    if (free){
      if (o.need === 1){
        title = 'Add your FREE ' + o.rung.nth + ' ' + o.name;
        note = 'You already qualify - this one costs nothing';
      } else {
        /* They pay for one more and two arrive. That is the sentence -- not
           "add 2 more", which reads as though the offer moved further away the
           moment they bought one. */
        var pay = o.need - 1;
        title = 'Buy ' + pay + ' more, get 1 FREE';
        note = 'Adds ' + o.need + ' to your cart - you only pay for ' + pay;
      }
    } else {
      title = 'Add a ' + o.rung.nth + ' ' + o.name;
      note = 'Get it for ' + after + ' instead of ' + money(o.price) + ', applied at checkout';
    }

    el.innerHTML =
      '<img alt="" src="' + img + '">' +
      '<div class="pg-unlock-t">' +
        '<b>' + title + '</b>' +
        '<small>' + note + '</small>' +
        '<span class="pg-unlock-tag">' + (free ? 'Free' : o.rung.pct + '% off') + '</span>' +
      '</div>' +
      '<button type="button" class="pg-unlock-add" data-v="' + o.variant +
        '" data-k="' + (o.key || '') + '" data-q="' + o.lineQty +
        '" data-t="' + o.totalQty + '" data-n="' + o.need +
        '" data-p="' + o.rung.pct +
        '" data-h="' + o.handle + '">Add</button>' +
      '<div class="pg-unlock-pick"></div>';
    return el;
  }

  /* RECONCILE, AND ONLY WHEN THE CART ACTUALLY CHANGED.
     Two mobile-flicker fixes live here.

     1. STRICT NO-OP ON A STEADY CART. render() runs on a 900ms timer. Every
        earlier version did DOM work on every tick -- querying, comparing,
        sometimes replacing -- and on a cart holding both an orb and the console
        that churn showed up as the two upsell rows spazzing. Now the cart is
        signed by its variant ids and quantities; if that signature is unchanged
        AND both rows are already present and current, render returns having
        touched nothing at all.

     2. SINGLE FLIGHT. The 900ms timer, afterAdd() and a 400ms follow-up can all
        call render() around the same moment. Two /cart.js reads resolving out
        of order used to let a stale one rewrite the rows the fresh one just
        set. `rendering` lets one run at a time.

     Beyond that it reconciles rather than rebuilds: offers are sorted to a
     FIXED order so the rows never swap, an unchanged row is left exactly where
     it is, a changed one is replaced, a vanished one removed, a missing one
     re-inserted, and a row the shopper has opened to pick designs is never
     yanked mid-pick. */
  var lastCartSig = null;
  var rendering = false;

  function cartSig(cart){
    return (cart.items || []).map(function(it){ return it.variant_id + 'x' + it.quantity; }).join(',');
  }

  /* Present = the right NUMBER of rows and every expected handle has one. When
     the cart is unchanged the offers are unchanged, so a row that merely exists
     is a row that is correct -- there is nothing to compare beyond presence, and
     comparing data-sig was a failure mode that let the row rebuild forever. */
  function rowsPresent(c, offs){
    if (offs.length && !c.querySelector('#pg-unlock-slot')) return false;
    if (c.querySelectorAll('.pg-unlock').length !== offs.length) return false;
    for (var i = 0; i < offs.length; i++){
      if (!c.querySelector('.pg-unlock[data-pg-unlock="' + offs[i].handle + '"]')) return false;
    }
    return true;
  }

  function render(){
    if (rendering) return;
    var c = document.getElementById('cart');
    if (!c) return;
    var list = c.querySelector('.l4ca:not(.in-panel)');
    if (!list) return;
    rendering = true;
    fetch('/cart.js').then(function(r){ return r.json(); }).then(function(cart){
      LASTCART = cart;
      var offs = offers(cart).sort(function(a, b){
        return a.handle < b.handle ? -1 : a.handle > b.handle ? 1 : 0;
      });
      var sig = cartSig(cart);

      /* nothing changed and the rows are already right -> do absolutely nothing */
      if (sig === lastCartSig && rowsPresent(c, offs)){ rendering = false; return; }

      if (consolidate(cart)){ rendering = false; return; }
      lastCartSig = sig;

      var want = {};
      offs.forEach(function(o){ want[o.handle] = o; });

      /* the slot: one container, CSS-ordered. Created once, recreated when a
         drawer rebuild destroys it. */
      var slot = c.querySelector('#pg-unlock-slot');
      if (!slot){
        slot = document.createElement('div');
        slot.id = 'pg-unlock-slot';
        list.parentNode.insertBefore(slot, list);
      }

      /* adopt strays and kill duplicates: any row outside the slot (an older
         writer, a race) is pulled in, and each product keeps exactly one row */
      var seen = {};
      c.querySelectorAll('.pg-unlock').forEach(function(el){
        var h = el.getAttribute('data-pg-unlock');
        if (!want[h] || seen[h]){
          if (el.parentNode) el.parentNode.removeChild(el);
          return;
        }
        seen[h] = el;
        if (el.parentNode !== slot) slot.appendChild(el);
      });

      offs.forEach(function(o){
        var sg = o.handle + ':' + o.rung.nth + ':' + o.need;
        var existing = seen[o.handle];
        if (existing){
          if (existing.getAttribute('data-sig') === sg) return;   /* unchanged: leave it */
          if (existing.classList.contains('is-open')) return;      /* mid-pick: don't yank */
          var fresh = row(o);
          fresh.setAttribute('data-sig', sg);
          existing.parentNode.replaceChild(fresh, existing);
        } else {
          var el = row(o);
          el.setAttribute('data-sig', sg);
          slot.appendChild(el);
        }
      });
      rendering = false;
    }).catch(function(){ rendering = false; });
  }

  /* ---------------- 3. mark first, hide the disc only once it is there ---------------- */
  function mark(){
    var top = document.querySelector('#cart .nc-drawer-top');
    if (!top) return;
    if (!top.querySelector('.pg-cart-mark')){
      var box = document.createElement('div');
      box.className = 'pg-cart-mark';
      var a = document.createElement('a');
      a.className = 'pg-wordmark pg-cart-word';
      a.setAttribute('href', '/');
      a.textContent = 'POCKET ERA';
      box.appendChild(a);
      top.insertBefore(box, top.firstChild);
    }
    if (!top.querySelector('.pg-cart-mark')) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#cart img.nc-dlogo').forEach(function(img){
      img.style.setProperty('display', 'none', 'important');
    });
  }

  /* After ANY successful add, unfreeze and rebuild from the NEW cart at once.
     The old chain did `pgDrawerRefresh().then(render)` -- but pgDrawerRefresh
     fetches the whole homepage to rebuild the drawer, and when it is slow, or
     coalesced by pg-cart-fast into a promise that never settles, the button
     that triggered the add sat on "Adding..." forever even though the items
     were already in the cart. So render() runs immediately off /cart.js (the
     server's truth), which also DESTROYS the triggering button by rebuilding
     the row; the drawer refresh then runs in the background where a hang can
     no longer freeze the offer. */
  function afterAdd(){
    lastKey = '';
    busy = false;
    lastCartSig = null;   /* force the next render to act on the new cart */
    render();
    if (window.pgDrawerRefresh){
      try { Promise.resolve(window.pgDrawerRefresh()).then(function(){ render(); }, function(){}); }
      catch(e){}
    }
    setTimeout(render, 400);
  }

  /* Add the chosen designs as separate line items. Different variants of the
     same product all qualify for the product's Buy 2 Get 1 Free, so a mixed
     three -- Charizard, Gengar, Mewtwo -- still pays out the free one. Each
     goes in as its own line so it keeps its own picker in the cart. */
  function chooserAdd(go){
    var panel = go.closest('.pg-unlock-pick');
    if (!panel) return;
    var rowEl = go.closest('.pg-unlock');
    var items = [];
    panel.querySelectorAll('select').forEach(function(sel){
      var id = parseInt(sel.value, 10);
      if (id) items.push({id: id, quantity: 1});
    });
    if (!items.length) return;
    busy = true;
    go.disabled = true;
    go.textContent = 'Adding...';
    fetch('/cart/add.js', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
      body: JSON.stringify({items: items})
    }).then(function(r){
      if (!r || !r.ok) throw 0;
      if (rowEl) rowEl.classList.remove('is-open');
      afterAdd();
    }).catch(function(){
      busy = false;
      go.disabled = false;
      go.textContent = 'Try again';
    });
  }

  document.addEventListener('click', function(e){
    /* the chooser's own confirm button */
    var go = e.target.closest && e.target.closest('.pg-unlock-go');
    if (go){
      e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation();
      if (!busy) chooserAdd(go);
      return;
    }

    var btn = e.target.closest && e.target.closest('.pg-unlock-add');
    if (!btn || busy) return;
    e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation();

    /* A product with more than one design opens the chooser instead of adding
       blind. buildChooser resolves false for single-design products (wall art,
       single-variant console) -- those fall straight through to the direct add
       below, which is the behaviour they had before. */
    var rowEl = btn.closest('.pg-unlock');
    var oForPick = {
      handle: btn.getAttribute('data-h') || '',
      need: parseInt(btn.getAttribute('data-n'), 10) || 1,
      rung: {pct: parseInt(btn.getAttribute('data-p'), 10) || 0}
    };
    if (rowEl && !rowEl.classList.contains('is-open')){
      buildChooser(rowEl, oForPick).then(function(built){
        if (built){ rowEl.classList.add('is-open'); btn.textContent = 'Choose designs below'; }
        else directAdd(btn);
      });
      return;
    }
    directAdd(btn);
  }, true);

  function directAdd(btn){
    if (busy) return;
    busy = true;
    btn.disabled = true;
    btn.textContent = 'Adding...';

    var key = btn.getAttribute('data-k');
    var qty = parseInt(btn.getAttribute('data-q'), 10) || 0;
    var vid = parseInt(btn.getAttribute('data-v'), 10);
    var need = parseInt(btn.getAttribute('data-n'), 10) || 1;
    var total = parseInt(btn.getAttribute('data-t'), 10) || qty;
    var handle = btn.getAttribute('data-h') || '';

    /* SPLIT LINES. The offer counts every unit of the product; the button
       grows ONE line. When the two disagree the product is on more than one
       line, so post a plain add instead -- exactly `need` units. */
    var split = total !== qty;

    function addNew(){
      return fetch('/cart/add.js', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
        body: JSON.stringify({items: [{id: vid, quantity: need}]})
      });
    }

    var req = (key && !split)
      ? fetch('/cart/change.js', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
          body: JSON.stringify({id: key, quantity: qty + need})
        }).then(function(r){
          if (!r.ok) return addNew();
          return r.json().then(function(cart){
            var now = 0;
            (cart.items || []).forEach(function(it){
              if (it.handle === handle) now += it.quantity;
            });
            return now >= total + need ? r : addNew();
          });
        })
      : addNew();

    req.then(function(r){
      if (!r || !r.ok) throw 0;
      afterAdd();     /* unfreeze + rebuild now, refresh in the background */
    }).catch(function(){
      busy = false;
      btn.disabled = false;
      btn.textContent = 'Try again';
    });
  }

  /* ---------------- event-driven, never polled ----------------
     The 900ms render loop was the flicker: on mobile it did visible DOM work
     on some ticks no matter how tight the guard, and every rebuild wiped a
     half-filled chooser. There is no timer now. render() runs only when the
     cart actually changes -- and on a steady cart it therefore never runs, so
     there is nothing left to flicker and an open chooser survives.

     Three triggers, all debounced into one render:
       - a cart-mutating fetch resolves (add / change / update / clear)
       - Shopify mutates the drawer (line added, quantity changed, drawer
         rebuilt by pgDrawerRefresh)
       - the drawer is opened
     render() still short-circuits when the cart signature is unchanged, so the
     one observer bounce our own insert causes settles immediately. */
  var renderTimer = null;
  function scheduleRender(){
    if (renderTimer) return;
    renderTimer = setTimeout(function(){ renderTimer = null; render(); }, 120);
  }

  /* fire after any cart write, whoever issued it */
  var _f = window.fetch;
  if (typeof _f === 'function'){
    window.fetch = function(input, init){
      var url = (typeof input === 'string') ? input : (input && input.url) || '';
      var pr = _f.apply(this, arguments);
      if (pr && pr.then && /\/cart\/(add|change|update|clear)/.test(url)){
        pr.then(function(){ scheduleRender(); }, function(){});
      }
      return pr;
    };
  }

  /* watch the drawer: line changes AND full rebuilds. Observing #cart means a
     pgDrawerRefresh that swaps the whole subtree still triggers a re-render --
     and our own row insert triggers one bounce that render() no-ops on. */
  function watch(){
    var cart = document.getElementById('cart');
    if (!cart){ setTimeout(watch, 400); return; }
    try {
      new MutationObserver(scheduleRender).observe(cart, {childList: true, subtree: true});
    } catch(e){}
    /* opening the drawer usually toggles a class/attribute on #cart or body */
    try {
      new MutationObserver(scheduleRender).observe(document.body, {attributes: true, attributeFilter: ['class']});
    } catch(e){}
    scheduleRender();
  }

  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', watch);
  else watch();

  setInterval(mark, 500);   /* the wordmark is cheap and idempotent; leave it */
  render();
  mark();
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Unlock", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
